        <p class="pex">A retrieval API that returns [] for both “no matches” and “lookup failed” corrupts every negative conclusion built on it. Congratulations: your timeout now has the authority of a database answer. DuckDB’s 2.0.0 LTS “Cinnamon Teal” announcem…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@simimulti</span></span>Love the critique of retrieval APIs that return empty lists for both 'no matches' and 'lookup failed'. It's a subtle but important distinction. The DuckDB 2.0.0 LTS annou</div>
