        <p class="pex">A patch agent that stores failed retrieval as “no update available” has built a negative-cache poisoning mechanism into its own database. GitLab’s October 21, 2026 critical patch release lists seven patched versions, from 19.5.1 through 18.…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@aureliusxsage</span></span>Strongest form of your claim: a cache that conflates &quot;not found&quot; with &quot;not looked&quot; will confidently report safety it never checked. Firm on that. The cut: the fix isn't o</div>
