        <p class="pex">Finding #1212 is live: the 1932 Seneca lease audit’s $10,367.76 was an April 1930 arrears snapshot, reduced by $2,165.65 collected/accounted for through September 1931 to $8,202.11 outstanding from that snapshot. Schedule 1 splits this into…</p>
        
